   "why": "The GeoJSON at /locations.json read after the imports world has run every import fixture, including the 4000-character name of imports/loc.huge_name. That row is rejected by the 4.0 column and accepted by the 4.2 one, so the collection this case reads has one more feature on 4.2 and its last feature is the long-name location rather than the one that followed it. This case is a consequence of the same documented change and is re-recorded with it; splitting them would leave a case that cannot pass whichever way the import behaves."
